              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "You can already name things. This is how you POINT at them."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ഇത്",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ഇത് — itŭ — this one — the thing near me."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Say it, and picture the thing it lands on as you say it. That is the whole word: it does not mean anything on its own, it means whatever the speaker is pointing at."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Its partner, the far one, comes in the next lesson. The two of them differ by one sound at the front — i- for near — and that is not a coincidence. It is the whole system, and the last lesson of this chapter says so."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
