            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "You can already name things. This is how you ASK about them."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ആര്",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ആര് — ārŭ — who? — asking about a person."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Say it with an asking voice. It points at no one: it asks your listener to name the person."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ārŭ opens with a long ā-. Do not hear it as the short a- of far that അത് atŭ and അവിടെ aviṭe share: it has nothing to do with distance. Tamil, next door, says yār; Malayalam's word is the same one with its first y- worn away."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "\"ആര് (ārŭ)\" three times, asking about a different person each time",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: \"ആര്\" three times, asking about a different person each time]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "it once with a word you already know after it",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: it once with a word you already know after it]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "RECALL",
              "instruction": "say neñcŭ",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU RECALL: say *neñcŭ*]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What is ārŭ? (who? — asking about a person.) Does its long ā- mean far, like the short a- of atŭ? (No — it is the same word as Tamil's yār, its y- worn away; it asks about a person.)"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
